The sum carries the projection. The sum of the two projections equals the projection of the sum subsystem.

Every neighbourhood of the larger sum is included in the master of the smaller sum: the master neighbourhood by the master equality, and a tagged neighbourhood by rewriting the factor master equality and composing the tagged inclusion with the embedding of the smaller master. Extensionality then matches the master, left-tag, and right-tag cases, ruling out an empty string in a tag and ruling out a cross-tag inclusion.
